 ## Overview
-The Bisection Method is an iterative root-finding algorithm used to refine the intersection position of a ray with an implicit surface within a specific segment identified by adaptive sampling. It serves as an alternative to the Secant method in ray marching pipelines, guaranteeing convergence by halving the search interval at each step. Unlike the Secant method, which uses linear interpolation between two points, the Bisection method relies solely on the sign of the field function evaluations to narrow the interval.
