 ## Background
-The Bisection Method is a classic root-finding algorithm. In the context of volume rendering and isosurface extraction, it is used as a refinement step after an initial coarse intersection is detected. It is often contrasted with the Secant method and the False Position method. The False Position method is described as a combination of linear interpolation and the midpoint algorithm, finding the exact intersection point even if the field function is not continuous, and is noted to be no worse than, and usually better than, the midpoint algorithm in terms of iteration count. [S2]
